<!--
  HANDOVER.md — Session-to-Session Relay Template
  
  This file is the relay baton between AI sessions. It captures:
    - What just happened (close blocks, in reverse chronological order)
    - What to do next (the note at the top)
    - What to avoid (the trap list, accumulating across sessions)
  
  Three discipline rules:
    1. Update this file LAST in any session — after all work is committed
    2. Read this file FIRST in any new session — before exploring code
    3. Trap list grows over time — never delete entries, only add
  
  Delete this comment block before committing.
-->

# [Project Name] — Session Handover

> **First thing in any new session: read this file, then [CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md).**
>
> If you're tempted to skip ahead and "just look at the code," don't. The 30 seconds you save will cost an hour later.

<!--
  Optional warning block for sub-project HANDOVERs in monorepos:
  
  > ⚠️ This is the [tool/feature/subproject] HANDOVER. The platform-level HANDOVER
  > at `docs/HANDOVER.md` may be stale relative to platform-level work.
  > For platform context: `git show main:docs/HANDOVER.md | head -70`
-->

