## 📝 Note to the next session ([prev session #] → [current session #])

Hi, I'm the agent from session [N].

### 🟢 How to start (don't overthink it, just do these in order)

1. Verify environment: `[command, e.g. `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`]`
2. Check git log: `git log --oneline -[N]` — top should be [expected commit description]
3. Install if needed: `[e.g. `pnpm install`]`
4. Read the session [N] close block below for full context
5. Open [path to current spec/issue] — that's your work
6. Start: [first concrete action, e.g. "RED → GREEN → /simplify → commit"]

### 💡 Lessons from this session

<!--
  What you learned that the next session should know but isn't a "trap" yet.
  Patterns, mental models, surprising-but-not-broken discoveries.
-->

- [Lesson 1 — e.g. "File-backed integration tests caught a bug in-memory tests missed"]
- [Lesson 2 — e.g. "Refactor to a record type when a function takes 3+ positional args"]
- [Lesson 3]

### ⚠️ Traps (carrying forward + [N] new this session)

<!--
  This list ACCUMULATES. Never delete entries — only add new ones at the bottom.
  Mark new entries with [new] so the next session can see what changed.
  
  After 30 sessions, this becomes the most valuable artifact in the project:
  a curated, battle-tested anti-pattern catalog.
-->

1. [Existing trap from session X — e.g. "`git add X && git commit` chain triggers the pre-commit hook in a way that loses staged files. Always do them as two separate commands."]
2. [Existing trap from session Y]
3. [Existing trap from session Z]
4. **[new]** [Trap discovered this session]
5. **[new]** [Another trap discovered this session]

### 🎯 What you're building this session

[One paragraph — what's the slice you're delivering?]

Concrete deliverables:
- [Deliverable 1]
- [Deliverable 2]
- [Deliverable 3]

[Optional: estimated cycles or time]

### ❓ Uncertain / needs alignment

<!--
  Things this session decided without full confidence.
  Surface them so the next session (or the human) can audit.
  
  This section is the antidote to AI's biggest hidden failure mode:
  making confident decisions on ambiguous input without flagging it.
-->

- [Decision 1 made on assumption — please verify before relying on it]
- [Question I couldn't resolve — needs human input]

Good luck.

— session [N] agent

